{#
  The person a page speaks for, in Markdown: what they wrote about themselves,
  then their links, one list item each. Prints nothing when the context has no
  `bio`. The note is Markdown already, so it is printed as written, with
  `markdownLinks` giving this site's links their `.md` URLs.

  `bio` is on an author archive and on the homepage of a site whose author is
  a user: `name`, `url`, `note` and `links` (each a `label` and a `url`). The
  header includes this file where the HTML draws the card, and a layout
  Markdown template may include it anywhere, such as a static front page's.
-#}
{% if bio %}
{% if bio.note %}
{{ bio.note | markdownLinks }}

{% endif %}
{% for link in bio.links %}
- [{{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
